1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
OCTO-EARTH is a hypothetical simulation of moving the Earth–Moon system outward
while tracking momentum, energy and a simplified habitability proxy.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Earth does not teleport. In the model it moves only through reaction to ejected mass.
Orbital changes are calculated from the evolving state; the viewer is not the physics engine.

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The selected reaction-mass enabler is access to a finite asteroid. Eight supporting arms
throw one packet together; the Earth–Moon system recoils. Fragments keep their velocities
and are tracked, not deleted.

4
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:27,000
A separate thin-film photovoltaic field is the modeled energy source. Supporting transmitters
and rectennas carry power to the arms. The ledger accounts for conversion losses, heat, spill
and packet energy; it does not certify a real power network.

5
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Five million collectors at half an AU intercept the configured 30 percent of solar output.
A separate mirror ring redirects sunlight to the simplified two-box climate model at the target.
Mirrors redirect light; they do not create energy.

6
00:01:49,000 --> 00:02:11,000
The orbit and energy traces come from simulation state. Earth’s atmospheric and space-weather
layers, clouds, winds and storms are illustrative. Climate is a global-mean proxy, not a full
Earth system or proof of habitability.

7
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The project’s internal criteria include orbital-plane inclination in degrees and an absolute
final eccentricity tolerance. They are not official tilt or eccentricity-change limits from the
supplied PDFs. The current PPO has not been retrained or evaluated on target hold.

8
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Four model screens fail their scale checks. At ten kilometres per second, ejecting one times ten to
the twenty-third kilograms from Earth yields only 169 metres per second; the ideal requirement is
about 4.11 times ten to the twenty-four kilograms.

9
00:02:48,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Forty-eight tests pass with one PyTorch-dependent device benchmark deselected; this sandbox lacks
the dependency. The physics-check entrypoint is also blocked by missing packages. Hardware,
structural safety and current RL performance remain unverified.
